<BaseLayout title="Community">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="section-kicker">A COLLABORATIVE INITIATIVE</div><h1>Stronger science<br /><em>through connection.</em></h1><p>QCD at FAIR brings together researchers across experimental collaborations, theory groups, and neighbouring scientific communities to shape a coherent hadron-physics programme.</p></section>
  <section class="section-wrap community-grid">
    <div class="community-lead"><span class="big-stat">100<span>+</span></span><h2>contributors.<br /><em>One shared vision.</em></h2><p>The White Paper reflects broad international input spanning hadron physics, nuclear physics, heavy-ion physics, theory, and astrophysics.</p></div>
    <div class="community-content"><article><span class="mini-label">CONNECT</span><h3>Across collaborations</h3><p>Build bridges between HADES, CBM, PANDA, and the wider GSI/FAIR community.</p></article><article><span class="mini-label">INTEGRATE</span><h3>Experiment meets theory</h3><p>Connect measurements with lattice QCD, effective field theories, continuum approaches, and phenomenology.</p></article><article><span class="mini-label">LOOK OUTWARD</span><h3>International synergies</h3><p>Develop complementary opportunities with hadron-physics programmes at facilities worldwide.</p></article></div>
  </section>
  <section class="join-band"><div><span class="section-kicker">GET INVOLVED</span><h2>Help shape the<br /><em>next chapter.</em></h2><p>Interested in contributing, sharing a result, or connecting a related activity? We welcome engagement from the broader community.</p></div><a class="button button-light" href="/contact/">Get in touch ↗</a></section>
</BaseLayout>
